Package: rinow
Type: Package
Title: Nowcasting of Indicators from Data Preparation to Evaluation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Achmad Syahrul", "Choir", email = "madsyair@stis.ac.id",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
    )
Description: Nowcasts a quarterly indicator, such as economic growth, from
    monthly indicators with one object-oriented interface that covers every
    stage of a nowcasting system: indicator metadata and release calendars,
    pseudo real-time data vintages with ragged edges, stationary
    transformations and temporal aggregation as in Mariano and Murasawa
    (2003) <doi:10.1002/jae.695>, and a common set of models. The models are
    bridge equations as in Baffigi, Golinelli and Parigi (2004)
    <doi:10.1016/S0169-2070(03)00067-0>, mixed data sampling regressions
    (Ghysels, Sinko and Valkanov (2007) <doi:10.1080/07474930600972467>;
    Foroni, Marcellino and Schumacher (2015) <doi:10.1111/rssa.12043>),
    diffusion indexes as in Stock and Watson (2002)
    <doi:10.1198/073500102317351921>, mixed-frequency dynamic factor models
    estimated with the Kalman filter as in Banbura and Modugno (2014)
    <doi:10.1002/jae.2306>, Bayesian vector autoregressions with
    conditional forecasts as in Giannone, Lenza and Primiceri (2015)
    <doi:10.1162/REST_a_00483>, a Bayesian dynamic factor model with
    Student-t errors and stochastic volatility in the spirit of
    Antolin-Diaz, Drechsel and Petrella (2024)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.105634>, machine-learning regressions as in
    Babii, Ghysels and Striaukas (2022) <doi:10.1080/07350015.2021.1899933>,
    and a bottom-up model that nowcasts expenditure components and
    aggregates them like the Atlanta Fed's GDPNow. Every model is evaluated
    in pseudo real time with the same schedule, accuracy measures,
    Diebold-Mariano tests with the correction of Harvey, Leybourne and
    Newbold (1997) <doi:10.1016/S0169-2070(96)00719-4>, and forecast
    combinations. An optional 'shiny' interface runs the workflow step by
    step. Example data for Indonesia are included. The name stands for
    nowcasting of indicators using R.
